WEBVTT

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.370
Have the player killers left
all the hunting grounds?

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:15.620
Yeah.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:22.700
You said Figaro would figure something
out about the PKs in the south.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.700
I wonder if he did anything
to clear out the others, too.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.700
Highly unlikely.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:30.040
Why's that?

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.660
Since he's based in Duel City,

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:36.120
he'd likely open up the southern
grounds, on the way there.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.040
But he has no reason
to clear out any other area.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:43.870
He did say it was a bother
that the road there was blocked.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:48.290
So why did all the other PKs vanish off the map?

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:51.830
Either they retreated once
the southern group got done in...

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:53.540
Or...

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:58.540
Or someone else just happened
to defeat them at the same time.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:00:59.870
I see.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:03.120
And you've hit the nail on the head!

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:42.160
"Chapter 3: 
Superior"

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.450
Um... and you are?

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.160
Oh, I beg your pardon!

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:44.580
This is who I am.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:51.410
"Name: Marie Adler"
"Job: Journalist"
"Affiliation: DIN"

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:49.750
Marie Adler... and your job is Journalist.

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:51.410
What's "DIN"?

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:55.790
It stands for " <i>Dendrogram</i> Information Network."

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.830
In old-school lingo, we're newshounds.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:01.330
If I'm being fancy,
we're a borderless information agency.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:03.830
Do you know the facts here?

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:06.080
Yeah! Want to hear 'em?

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.250
Information isn't free, you know.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:13.830
I'll pay.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:17.290
Oh, Ray, I'll cover half.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:20.450
Much obliged!

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.410
Let's start at the end.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:25.080
The bands of player killers that had
occupied the hunting grounds

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:30.160
in all four corners of the kingdom
are now paying the penalty for dying.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.200
Bands?

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.160
That's right.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:37.410
K&R in the east, Mad Castle in the south,
and Goblin Street in the west:

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:40.870
"Mad Castle"

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:40.870
"Goblin Street"

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:40.870
These three PK clans had staked their claims.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:43.410
Huh? What about the north, where I was killed?

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:46.120
And who defeated them?

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:50.200
Masters who'd evolved their
Embryos to their seventh form.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.750
These four Superiors,
affiliated with the Kingdom of Altar,

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:57.120
sprang into action to wipe out
the player killer clans.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.540
Superiors...

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:01.250
King of Destruction, the Unknown.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:03.040
Figaro, the Endless Chain.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:05.370
Tsukuyo Fuso of the Lunar World.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:07.620
Lei-Lei, the Prodigal of Feasts.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.660
Each of these four wiped out one clan apiece.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:15.950
What's this?

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:18.500
A video, of sorts.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:24.290
What you are about to see
are certain portions of this event.

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:28.120
Let's start in the south, shall we?

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:34.910
That's right--run!

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:47.540
Do just one point of damage to me,
boy, and I'll let you go.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.580
Our boss is one mean dude!

00:04:58.580 --> 00:04:59.790
He sure is!

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:03.120
He's using Damage Decrease
and Damage Reduction--

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:09.660
try as he might, that kid'll never do
a lick of damage to the ol' bossman.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.500
Okay, time's up!

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:26.870
<i>Damn</i> , I love being a player killer!

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:30.830
That 10K lir per player is pretty sweet!

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:35.410
But we ain't gettin' many players lately.
Mebbe they're scared.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:38.290
I know the gang out east
is twiddlin' their thumbs.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:43.410
The western gang is still hunting
tians, too. Business is booming!

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:46.160
That bunch is so nuts, it's scary.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.120
I'm more interested in the north.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:51.330
The north? Let's see, um...

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:54.160
There's no gang in the north--
it's just one person.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.410
And their name is--

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.410
Boss!

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.870
Fresh meat incoming!

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.660
Ah! Send them our way.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:05.370
Roger that! This one looks real--

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:09.370
"Joke α has logged out as a penalty for dying"

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:09.370
Joke α has logged out as a penalty for dying.

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:11.750
Huh? True to your name, eh, Jo--

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:17.700
Loward Beltmars has logged out
as a penalty for dying.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:17.700
Dread Murdaw has logged out
as a penalty for dying.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:18.700
"Killing Intent Perception"

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:20.200
Astro Guard!

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.000
Tch. Instant defeat.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:30.790
Still, what can damage a foe who's quintupled
his defense with Astro Guard?

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.370
This chain attack...

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:39.500
So many roadblocks today.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:43.080
The Over Gladiator--Figaro!

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:47.870
Are you an Armor Giant?
You've got great defense.

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:50.330
You don't see that kind of toughness very often.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:53.700
Is your Embryo built for defense, too?

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:59.040
Looks like I've taken care
of all the other player killers.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:04.200
Oh, and... you're their boss?

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:06.040
What if I am?

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:10.120
I just want to get traffic moving here again,

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:13.120
so if you retreat, I'll let you live.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:18.620
Equipping multiples of special
Unique Boss Monster weapons

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:21.540
like it's no big deal...

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:26.000
Can't steal them--it'd be
a tough fight, and for what?

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:30.370
Understood. Mad Castle will withdraw completely.

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:33.200
Oh, really? Great.

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:37.080
I do have this Contract. Should we use it?

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:40.120
Yes, let's. Since you have one and all.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:46.620
"Barbaroy."

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.790
There, done. Take a look.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:56.040
Once someone like you
shows up, I mean, it's time.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:57.330
Four meters.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:00.000
Our members are all wiped out.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.290
Three meters.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:04.450
Really, all we can do at this point is retreat.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:08.580
After killing <i>you</i> , that is!

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:12.580
Heaven's Weight!

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:10.540
"Heaven's Weight"

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:20.080
Figures you wouldn't be crushed to death!

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:23.950
But now it's time for
my Embryo's ultimate skill!

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:26.330
Astro Guard!

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:31.160
Atlas!

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:31.160
"Emancipated Giant -- Atlas"

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:36.290
This converts defensive power
to offensive power--

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:39.870
and boosts offense tenfold for just ten seconds!

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:44.160
Even if you <i>are</i> a Superior,
a direct blow means instant death!

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:50.830
Shatter and die!

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.450
Hah!

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:01.950
Th-This is ridiculous!
That was 500 times standard gravity!

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:20.950
C-Can't... breathe...

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:26.000
Could all this nonsense be thanks
to his Superior Embryo?

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:33.200
It's a <i>game</i> ! With no pain perception! And yet...

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:36.790
I can feel myself falling!

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:52.620
That was an incredibly brutal fight.

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:58.330
Thus Mad Castle came to a bitter end.

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:01.750
Now for the east.

00:10:12.450 --> 00:10:14.330
Wh-What the...?

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:16.450
The Lunar Society...

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:08.500
She heads the Lunar Society clan--
which is a religious sect in Japan.

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:12.540
Founder of the Lunar Society: Tsukuyo Fuso.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.750
Why bring it into the game?

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:25.620
As the first tenet of her religion says:
"Depart your shackled physical body

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:28.950
for a new world of the soul."

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:33.910
I imagine she thought <i>Dendro</i>
was that "new world of the soul."

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:39.080
Wouldn't she have fulfilled
that belief as soon as she arrived?

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:41.160
Then you have their <i>second</i> tenet:

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:46.330
"Revel in a world of freedom
to your very soul's content."

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:48.250
Something like that.

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:53.410
Incidentally, she only joined the anti-PK effort

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:56.750
because they picked off
one of her newbie believers.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:12:02.910
And that gets the whole clan
after you? Terrifying!

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:09.580
Next up: The west.

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:38.080
Jeez, talk about terrifying!

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:40.790
That's Lei-Lei, Prodigal of Feasts.

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:45.250
Has a nasty habit of poisoning newbies
with an alcohol lookalike.

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:49.290
We don't know why she joined the PK rout.

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:51.620
Now, the last one is up north.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.120
The north...

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:59.700
Um, who exactly was
the player killer in the north?

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:05.700
The identity of the PK in Noz Forest is unknown.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:07.620
They're a Superior Killer.

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:09.830
A Superior Killer...

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:13.700
Here, let me play the video.

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:27.660
Er, isn't this--?

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:30.160
Just watch, okay?

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.620
Here! Watch this part right here!

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:39.410
That shadow...

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:42.450
The mysterious King of Destruction.

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:48.160
We have it on good authority
that his Embryo is a battleship.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:51.830
That's a thing, huh?

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:54.000
Well, it's all rumors, anyway.

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:59.160
I doubt even that unidentified Superior Killer
stood a chance against <i>that</i> spectacle.

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:03.200
As it turns out, despite those flames
blasting Noz Forest to cinders,

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:07.000
the Superior Killer made it out in one piece.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.750
Huh...

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:12.500
That's good news, indeed.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:17.500
They're still alive.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:26.870
So this is the power of the King of
Destruction--and his Superior Embryo.

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:29.790
I understand the Knights put out the fire.

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:37.620
You're a Paladin now, Ray--
the least you could do is pitch in.

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:46.290
This Superior Killer managed
to escape a forest-leveling attack.

00:14:46.290 --> 00:14:48.870
We should be grateful they did.

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:51.330
After all, we <i>did</i> swear
we'd defeat them ourselves.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:54.290
We sure did.

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:55.580
What's that?

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:58.620
Hey, Nemesis, what's up?

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:00.910
Wha--? Nemesis!

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:20.080
What took you so long?

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:24.910
Cheshire?

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:34.080
What are you doing here, Cheshire?

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:36.790
Environmental maintenance prep, you might say.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:39.910
Though it's not strictly my job.

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:46.040
I'm surprised to see the two of <i>you</i> here.
Players can't normally get in.

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:47.160
Really?

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:48.500
Yes, really.

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:51.870
Although it looks like you've got
a Maiden Embryo there.

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:54.290
I suppose this kind of thing can happen.

00:15:54.290 --> 00:15:56.750
What's different about a Maiden?

00:15:56.750 --> 00:15:59.370
They're closer to us in some ways.

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:02.040
They retain ***** functionality, for example.

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:05.080
Huh? What was that again?

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:08.950
Sorry! That data couldn't be put into words.

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:12.950
It's no big deal. Just forget about it.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.250
Some duty of confidentiality?

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:23.000
So you're going to fix up this area, then?

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.120
Well, we won't recreate it directly.

00:16:25.120 --> 00:16:30.000
But we'll make it easier to build
a similar environment.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.700
I see.

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:38.410
We won't engage directly with the marks
that autonomous acts leave on this world.

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:42.120
Although the control AI
for punishments is an exception.

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:43.500
Punishments?

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:46.410
If player killers aren't punished, who is?

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:50.790
Hmm. Someone on a country's
most-wanted list, say?

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:56.910
A player in state custody can always log out
or die and come back a free person.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:59.950
We do have player gaol, you know.

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:01.370
Makes sense.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:05.620
If the penalty for dying were the only
punishment, you'd get repeat offenders.

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:10.750
Even someone on the most-wanted list
has to be defeated before they can be jailed.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:14.500
Which means the toughest criminals
would remain at large.

00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:22.540
It's been a while since I've met
with anyone in this form--

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:24.830
apart from registration, that is.

00:17:24.830 --> 00:17:27.540
Wish I could give you something
to mark the occasion,

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:30.540
but that's a no-no for us admin types.

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:34.120
That's all right. We did have tea and snacks.

00:17:34.120 --> 00:17:35.000
Thanks!

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:37.080
Yeah--it was delectable!

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:39.540
You've got something on your face.

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:45.080
Oh, right: You're headed
for Gideon, was it, Ray?

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:48.700
Yes. I need to thank someone out that way.

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:50.370
Well, be careful.

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:53.660
Oh? Any particular reason?

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:57.370
Let me just say this as tactfully as possible:

00:17:57.370 --> 00:18:00.250
The ogre's heart is in its stomach.

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:01.290
Huh?

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:04.040
Something to keep in mind.

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:07.620
I hope we'll run into each other again sometime!

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:23.580
This is seriously a ton of requests.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:24.950
It really is.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:29.950
With the roads open again, there's been
a surge in merchant security requests.

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:34.620
Hey, I've been meaning to ask--
what job did you take, Rook?

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:35.660
Pimp!

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:38.160
Pimp? That's a job here?

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:39.870
What skills does that have?

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:42.870
I've got these so far.

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:49.450
"Job: Pimp"
Skills: Male Temptation
Female Monster Enhancing"

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:45.830
I'm sensing a theme here.

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:49.450
Maybe Pimp is some kind of monster-taming job.

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:52.330
Something like that...

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:56.870
Now, I can't have you show me
yours without showing mine.

00:18:56.870 --> 00:19:00.830
Paladin's Aegis and Instant Wield?
How cool is that?!

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:06.750
Say, can Nemesis use Counter Absorption
and Vengeance Is Mine on her own?

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:09.160
Not Vengeance Is Mine.

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:12.790
For that, I become a weapon and am equipped.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:14.950
Oh, is that right?

00:19:14.950 --> 00:19:17.040
But hey, Master, check this out!

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:20.580
The big-money boss monsters
Lobohta, King of the Pack,

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:25.040
and Great Miasmic Ogre Gardranda
can show up on the road to Gideon!

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:26.370
I hope we see them!

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:29.870
I'm not big on such blatant danger...

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:31.290
Say, Rook!

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:36.330
Wouldn't the Special Pudding à la Mode
be yummy with Death Sauce?

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:37.870
You want some, too?

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:41.410
I'm not big on such blatant danger...

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:45.290
Huh?

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:51.790
Stands to reason.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:57.330
When three of the five of us
are stunners, we'll draw attention.

00:19:57.330 --> 00:19:58.370
Wait...

00:19:58.370 --> 00:19:59.620
<i>Five</i> ?!

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:04.120
Where'd <i>you</i> come from?
And what are you doing here?

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.910
I just happened to have some business in Gideon.

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:09.450
I figured I'd pick up a request along the way

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:13.000
when I heard you two discussing
your own trip to Gideon.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:15.910
And well, I just <i>had</i> to tag along.

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:19.410
I don't particularly mind. What about you, Rook?

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:22.870
That's fine by me. I'd feel better, actually.

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:27.120
True. It'll be the first time
we've traveled to another city.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:31.950
I'm used to long-distance travel.
Leave it to me!

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:34.450
Okay, how about this one?

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:36.620
A level 2 quest.

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:43.500
Deliver goods from the local Guild
to the one in Gideon. For 30 thousand lir!

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:45.080
I like the sound of that.

00:20:45.080 --> 00:20:46.580
Okay by you, Marie?

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:48.620
Just dandy!

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:49.910
Then it's settled.

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:54.250
Is it? But Babi hasn't had her pudding yet!

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:57.040
Okay, I'll go sign us up.

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:06.750
Let's split up for today.
We'll head out tomorrow morning.

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:08.750
You don't have any plans, do you?

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:11.830
No--nothing in particular.

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:15.620
I'm fine, too, seeing as
I'm jobless at the moment.

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:21.410
Then we start our quest tomorrow!

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:30.910
Goblins?

00:21:30.910 --> 00:21:33.160
A-And so many of them!

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:36.620
There's no way we can handle this crowd, sir!

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:38.790
Just take the cart and go!

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:48.290
Are they trying to intimidate us?

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:51.870
Looks like we'll ma--

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:59.080
Wh-What?!

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:01.540
It can't be...

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:02.950
Gardran--

00:23:43.910 --> 00:23:48.370
"Like a Flag Flying the Reversal"

00:23:45.450 --> 00:23:47.620
"Like a Flag Flying the Reversal."
